rectangle "MORE THAN ENOUGH\n<size:16>[Software System]</size>" <<Boundary-TU9SRSBUSEFOIEVOT1VHSA==>> {
  rectangle "Simulation Core\n<size:16>[Container: JavaScript modules (browser + Node)]</size>" <<Boundary-U2ltdWxhdGlvbiBDb3Jl>> {
    rectangle "==Layered World\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nCoordinates and key packing (x, y, z), tile rules as data (TILE_INFO), and chunked terrain: the forest surface at z = 0 from noise octaves, solid geology below with one shaft per chunk. Chunks are generated lazily and LRU-cached; player edits (richness mods), per-layer fog and the holes between layers live outside the cache. Explored chunks and observed resource types have derived spatial indexes, including one/two-unit reserve masks that remove exhausted deposits from searches; Map-compatible prop mutation epochs invalidate charger candidates." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsQ29yZSBFbmdpbmU=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.SimulationCore.LayeredWorld
    rectangle "==Simulation Step\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nstep(s, dt): production, logistics, abundance income, battery and the burning flare; movement and fog reveal as far as your light reaches (sightRadius). Browser and AUTO hosts enable cumulative solo production after Logistics: grouped rates, cached counts/mastery, command/query settlements, and buffer snapshots at saves or rate changes. Visual events query nearby tile buckets. Cultivation runs local environment deadlines at 250ms in the same canonical step. Battery intervals support quiet-tick batching and reuse nearby charger candidates with exact range and daylight checks. Reveal compares exact circle row intervals and visits newly covered edges. Resource streams settle together with targeted manual balance updates. Variable-step/shared callers and extreme arithmetic retain the legacy economy." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsQ29yZSBFbmdpbmU=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.SimulationCore.SimulationStep
    rectangle "==Actions\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nHarvest (gather deposits on the surface, dig rock underground), Trail sweep targets, collect, and build; plus travel between layers through holes (dig down from the forest, climb up through the ceiling, drop through holes and shafts). All work on the player's own layer." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsQ29yZSBFbmdpbmU=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.SimulationCore.Actions
    rectangle "==AUTO Brain\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nnextIntent(s, mind): legal player actions from explored terrain, remembered observations, visible mine glints, own resources and public rules. Integer A* treats unseen underground rock as an assumption and replans after normal revelation, without inspecting hidden geology. Unseen chargers, ladders, shores and tunnel props cannot steer decisions. Prices building repayment against required upgrades; mining is a fallback only when surface acquisition is unavailable, includes passive income and return travel and targets useful observed finds. Waits at Embark, and never spends Insight in shared worlds. Selected known chargers alone authorize charging decisions. Manual holds share AUTO cadence. Pure: mind caches observations and routes." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsQ29yZSBFbmdpbmU=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.SimulationCore.AUTOBrain
  }

  rectangle "Web Application\n<size:16>[Container: HTML/CSS/JavaScript modules]</size>" <<Boundary-V2ViIEFwcGxpY2F0aW9u>> {
    rectangle "==AUTO\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nThe AUTO button (formerly Perfect): while held (and no sheet or dialog is up, and the player isn't steering, gathering or working a tile) it asks the brain for the next intent about four times a second and has the Controller carry it out, the same calls a tap makes. Keeps the badge (what it's doing), waits at Embark with a toast, and keeps the screen awake while held." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.AUTO
    rectangle "==Camera\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nMaps world (x, y, height) to screen pixels and back (project/unproject) with zoom and a fixed slight lean; picking hits the top or face you see. Also the visible tile range." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.Camera
    rectangle "==Renderer\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nPaints all floor tiles before standing objects in north-to-south row order. Local viewport-bounded masks preserve higher foreground terrain occlusion without clipping feet against equal-height floor. The faint visibility pass omits character and boat shadows; placement ghosts share the masks, Wiki focus and map mode retain their independent paths, and renderer fault recovery restores canvas clipping. The default player is Mica, a compact flat orange-hooded repairer with skinned split coat/patch, explicit-time mesh-eye blinks and curious idle/recovery poses, actual-cargo protective carrying and localized inspection, with eight snapped world headings: twenty-one bone hierarchy with four weighted cloak panels, one-handed mining from the shaft's end and fixed-length arm IK to the WORK_HANDS targets in work-motion.js, earned palm-bound baskets and belt lanterns from work-equipment.js, free-hand assembly and a one-cycle coalescing actor queue with captured work facing, torso and head counterbalance, articulated elbows and wrists, and pure two-bone leg IK plus layered action curves from rig-motion.js. rig-model.js builds the rig without a renderer and names its solids and their joints and grips; rig-clips.js finds crossing triangles between them, which the unit sweep and the local dev build treat as a fault. rigged-character.js lazily bundles vendored Three.js and reuses one 320x448 WebGL surface composited into the 2D canvas. Wiki, a four-bone mycelium sprite with a skinned folding cap (wiki-model.js, pure pose in wiki-motion.js), rides the hood bone in the same pass and outline; src/game/wiki.js decides what it looks at and says (a long press on the map asks it), and focus.js rings what it talks about in Wiki teal around the whole object. pickaxe-model.js supplies cached six-tier palm/back equipment and offline-baked matching icons, one flat fill mesh per tier with no ink shell; the character contour outlines it while equipped and a 2D silhouette stamp outlines the icons. Action/boat feedback shares canonical timing; presentation never runs simulation ticks. Mica is not drawn while the rig loads; without WebGL and for friends, the 2D wanderer stands in. A cached multisampled color target and one alpha-derived screen-space ink pass outline the complete figure, replacing per-piece hulls. Exact sRGB fills are preserved, with no CPU readback in normal rendering. Geometry, combined-pass draw calls and compressed module size are bounded. resource-models.js builds four canonical 3D materials and offline vector views through scripts/resource-art.mjs; icons/deposits/small piles remain cached texture-pack SVGs at runtime, flat value planes over one whole-object ink silhouette with no face or part edges. No player text." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.Renderer
    rectangle "==Main Loop\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nWires the modules together and owns the current state (game.state, replaced on embark/reset). Schedules the shared fixed-tick engine independently of drawing. Each simulation tick steers, steps the Core, reveals fog, works held input and ticks AUTO; presentation separately updates effects, save/HUD timers and rendering. A frame, a drawing layer or a tap that throws is skipped and kept as a problem report (faults.js, problems.js); only frames failing in a row stop the game. Exposes window.MTE_GAME for the browser tests." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.MainLoop
    rectangle "==Tick and Deadline Engine\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nShared 60 Hz logical clock. Browser catch-up is bounded; the headless runner coalesces stationary ticks ending at AUTO/goal deadlines, retaining fine motion and first Embark eligibility. Cumulative battery intervals preserve daylight transitions. Injected controller, AUTO and input interfaces keep scheduling independent of presentation. Blocked UI suspends AUTO-owned movement." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.TickandDeadlineEngine
    rectangle "==Controller\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nApplies intents to the game: tap (descend, harvest, collect, or walk there round obstacles: planWalk/walkAim in core paths.js, replanned when a hoped-open route through fog turns out blocked), Gather (collect, else harvest, else Explore walks to the nearest resource) and its hold, AUTO's intents (perform), Trail sweeps (every way of working a tile takes turns on one hand clock, core pace.js), going down and up between layers, buying, building, embarking, resetting. Each calls the Core, then triggers effects, sound, HUD and a save." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.Controller
  }

